0..46 Comment "//! Vectors are lists indexed by their length."
47..50 Comment "//!"
51..128 Comment "//! A vector\'s type states its length. A function then states the length that"
129..144 Comment "//! it returns."
145..148 Comment "//!"
149..225 Comment "//! The kind `Nat -> Type` reads the type of the length before the universe."
226..305 Comment "//! `VNil` stands at zero. `VCons` stands at one past the length of its tail. A"
306..384 Comment "//! length written as a call stands at the length that the call computes. Thus"
385..465 Comment "//! `plus(m, Zero)` is the length `m`. The pathological twin holds the refusals."
466..469 Comment "//!"
470..552 Comment "//! - cites: [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families] — a family whose constructors each"
553..588 Comment "//!   state the index they stand at"
589..671 Comment "//! - see: #3579 — a family\'s argument written as a call converts with its value"
672..750 Comment "//! - see: #3625 — a constructor\'s field written as a call meets a type that"
751..772 Comment "//!   writes the call"
773..851 Comment "//! - see: #3627 — a constructor at a length written as a call that computes"
852..878 Comment "//!   the length it states"
879..882 Comment "//!"
883..984 Comment "//! [Dybjer-1994-inductive_families]: https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01211308 \"Dybjer, Inductive families\""
986..1023 Comment "// The naturals the lengths count in."
